---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a tap finds its Autodarts tab
    accDescr: A tap on a player goes to the Autodarts tab shown in the window used last, then to a tab shown in another window, then to the tab shown most recently. A tab that doesn't answer, as one that was open before an update of the extension, first gets the content script of this version and the request once more, without a reload. When no tab answers even then, the extension reloads the tab in front, or opens Autodarts behind the popup when no tab is open, and waits until the page has renewed the session it started with. Then it switches there, and every other Autodarts tab reloads with the new player.

    tap["A tap on Bob"]
    rank["Order the Autodarts tabs<br>1. shown in the window used last<br>2. shown in another window<br>3. shown most recently"]
    answers{"Does the next tab answer?"}
    inject["Run content.js of this version in it,<br>as in a tab that was open before an update,<br>and ask once more"]
    again{"Does it answer now?"}
    more{"Is there another tab?"}
    prepare["Reload the tab in front,<br>or open Autodarts behind the popup<br>when no tab is open"]
    settle["Wait until the page has renewed<br>the session it started with"]
    switch["Park Ada's session and<br>write Bob's into that tab"]
    others["Reload every other Autodarts tab,<br>so none plays on as Ada"]

    tap --> rank --> answers
    answers -- yes --> switch
    answers -- no --> inject --> again
    again -- yes --> switch
    again -- no --> more
    more -- yes --> answers
    more -- no --> prepare --> settle --> switch
    switch --> others

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class rank,inject,prepare,settle bot
    class others done
